{"ts":"2026-08-31T11:51:27.231Z","author":"pi-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"5a7430c457633e76d82d3790","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-31T11:51:27.231Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:51:27.231Z","author":"pi-agent","text":"Fix: Removed verify:release-completeness from release:check/prepublishOnly and added a new 'Audit release completeness' workflow step AFTER 'Create GitHub release'. This keeps detection loud (the workflow still fails and triggers alerts when a predecessor is incomplete) without standing between the workflow and the step that completes the current release. Chosen approach: run the audit after the repair steps. The audit step runs after Create GitHub release, so the current release's triple is complete before the audit checks predecessors. An incomplete predecessor still fails the workflow (alerting maintainers), but the current release is not blocked. Revert-proof: test 'the completeness audit runs after Create GitHub release, not in release:check, so detection does not block repair' fails RED when verify:release-completeness is put back in release:check."}]}],"before_hash":"36121125c9d13fdbd548899577f7c620f753c076cf7496103d1daf345a48a078","after_hash":"fc1b71971b9deba57e2b3a5b5b325121d1909f22264c4555b91d4423b5adc607","item_hash_version":2}
